        <OtherAbstract Type="PIP" Language="eng">
            <AbstractText>Vacuum curettage of the uterus without anesthesia has been tested in gynecological surgery as an alternative to conventional abrasio under anesthesia. In a questionnaire, the patients investigated described the pains they felt and decided on the method to be used in the event of a possible future curettage. Most women find the method more or less painful but nevertheless prefer it to curettage under anesthesia. It therefore has a definite place in the gynecological work done in outpatient departments. (Author's modified)</AbstractText>
        </OtherAbstract>
